    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0242" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/3528: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-14T19:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Your 71, October 13, 7 P.M.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d133-f1"/> Dunn is
                    apparently wrong in thinking that first series 1926 bonds have prior lien over
                    second series. Our records indicate and banker’s circular specifically states
                    second series rank equally with first series. Please consult and advise basis of
                    Dunn’s statement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stemson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
